# Cursor AI Rules

## Project Overview

This is a Next.js 16 application with AI capabilities. Follow these guidelines when working with this codebase.

---

## General Guidelines

1. **Write clean, readable code** - Code is read more often than written
2. **Follow existing patterns** - Consistency over personal preference
3. **Think before generating** - Understand the context and requirements
4. **Test your changes** - Verify functionality before committing

---

## Language & Framework Rules

### TypeScript
- Always use strict type checking
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes
- Use `const` assertions for immutable values
- Avoid `any` - use `unknown` when type is uncertain
- Enable all strict compiler options

### React & Next.js
- Use functional components with hooks
- Default to Server Components
- Use `'use client'` only when necessary
- Implement proper loading and error states
- Use dynamic imports for code splitting

### Styling (Tailwind CSS)
- Use utility classes directly in JSX
- Follow mobile-first responsive design
- Use CSS variables for theming
- Implement dark mode with `dark:` prefix
- Keep responsive classes in order: base → sm → md → lg → xl

---

## Code Style

### File Naming
```
components/
├── ui/
│   ├── button.tsx          # kebab-case for files
│   └── input.tsx
├── features/
│   ├── user-profile.tsx
│   └── product-card.tsx
```

### Component Structure
```tsx
// 1. Imports (grouped)
import { useState } from 'react';
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';

// 2. Types
interface ComponentProps {
  title: string;
  className?: string;
}

// 3. Component
export function Component({ title, className }: ComponentProps) {
  // Hooks at the top
  const [state, setState] = useState(null);
  
  // Handlers
  const handleClick = () => {};
  
  // Render
  return (
    <div className={cn('base-styles', className)}>
      {title}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Function Guidelines
```typescript
// ✅ Good: Small, focused functions
function validateEmail(email: string): boolean {
  const emailRegex = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
  return emailRegex.test(email);
}

// ✅ Good: Pure functions when possible
function calculateTotal(items: CartItem[]): number {
  return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price * item.quantity, 0);
}

// ✅ Good: Early returns for clarity
function getUserStatus(user: User | null): string {
  if (!user) return 'guest';
  if (user.isAdmin) return 'admin';
  return 'member';
}
```

